    {
      "id": "key-text",
      "shape": "text",
      "role": "label",
      "face": "body",
      "text": "Blue: Ravel processes. Grey: caller.\nThis example sends INT directly to the Ravel CLI; it is not keyboard delivery.\nHUP and TERM give shell statuses 129 and 143 by the same cancellation rule.\nA failed signal propagation uses the corresponding numeric exit as fallback.\nCancellation reports attempted teardown, not a guarantee that cleanup succeeded.",
